<title>UK: Shell rules out bid for British Gas - paper.</title>
<headline>Shell rules out bid for British Gas - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell Group is not interested in a takeover bid for British Gas, according to Cor Herkstroter, chairman of the Anglo-Dutch company, the Independent newspaper said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking at many opportunities for takeovers, but not at British Gas,&quot; the newspaper quoted Herkstroter as saying. Separately, a company spokesman ruled out using Royal Dutch/Shell's 7.0 billion stg ($11.7 billion) of reserves to fund a share buy-back, the newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The spokesman said Royal Dutch/Shell share buy-backs were very difficult in the Netherlands.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom + 44 171 542 4367</p>
